## TODO: nexus-detail-parity

Verified presentation gaps on the Nexus detail page, smallest-first. All API facts
live-verified 2026-08-07 unless marked.

- Per-file changelogs: v2 modFiles.changelogText ([String], live-populated) - render
  in DownloadsTab per file. Mod-level: v1 changelogs.json (doc-verified,
  version -> notes map) can back a Changelog tab like ModWorkshop's. Both authed.
- Version in browse/search: add version to SEARCH_QUERY (live-verified populated) -
  gate behind the nexus-update-detection coordination note.
- Uploader row: uploader { name, memberId, avatar } (live) + profile link
  nexusmods.com/users/{memberId} through shell_open_external.
- Bigger images where the UI already wants them: thumbnailLargeUrl exists (live);
  pictureUrl stays the detail hero.
- ADULT CONTENT - currently a real gap, raise priority: adult mods are returned by
  DEFAULT to unauthenticated/unfiltered queries (live: 12 adult S2 mods,
  totalCount, with adultContent flags) and Modrex neither selects the flag nor
  filters, so adult thumbnails render unblurred today. Fix: select adultContent
  everywhere, default to excluding adult results via the ModsFilter adultContent
  predicate (matching the site's signed-out default), and when shown, use
  thumbnailBlurredUrl / thumbnailLargeBlurredUrl (both exist precisely for this) with
  an explicit reveal. UNRESOLVED: whether authed results auto-respect the account's
  content preferences (needs a signed-in test; question 4 in nexus-policy-boundaries).
  Tests: filter predicate presence, blurred-variant selection, reveal gating.
- GALLERY: API-BLOCKED, verified two-sided - Mod carries no image-list field, and the
  v2 media query cannot filter by mod (MediaSearchFilter has gameId/type/owner only),
  so a mod's site gallery is not reachable. Scraping the website for it is NOT an
  acceptable fallback (AUP; see nexus-policy-boundaries). Single pictureUrl stays the
  honest ceiling until Nexus answers question 2. If they expose it later: disk-cache
  via the thumbnails full-URL-keying work, CSP already allows staticdelivery/images
  hosts - re-audit both csp and devCsp at that point.

Modules: nexus.rs (selection sets), domain.rs (wire fields), ModDetailPage /
DownloadsTab / NexusBrowsePage, i18n. Sequencing: any of these can ship independently;
none needs the source restructure.

