## TODO: index-multi-source

Phase 6 of the multi-source expansion. Work spans apps/index and apps/desktop.

### Context

The Postgres schema already has a `sources` table (games -> sources -> mods ->
files), and export-sqlite.ts already carries source columns into each snapshot,
but apps/desktop's queries (mod_index.rs) filter by game name only and return a
bare remote id the app assumes is a modworkshop id. Cross-posting is common
(authors publish the same file to Nexus + mod.io + modworkshop), so one SHA256
will match multiple identities.

Note this is now the last remaining place where the app assumes modworkshop from
a bare id. The INSTALLED side was fixed separately: InstalledMod carries an
explicit `source` plus a string `remoteId`, and its numeric `id` is an opaque
source-scoped key. The index reader is the holdout.

### What to do

- mod_index.rs lookups return `(source, remote_id)`; callers stop assuming
  modworkshop. Precedence policy for multi-source SHA256 hits: prefer the source
  the mod was installed from (InstalledMod.source now makes this answerable),
  else a fixed priority order.
- apps/index gains per-source fetchers. Constraint: the "download everything
  and hash SHA256" strategy is modworkshop-shaped. Nexus ToS will not tolerate
  mass-downloading, but Nexus offers an MD5 lookup API - identification there
  wants MD5, which means per-source identification strategies and possibly
  dual-hashing (SHA256 + MD5) installed files in apps/desktop going forward.
  Steam Workshop hashing would require steamcmd-driven downloads.
- Keep the hard rule from builder-state: zero-yield mods never become `mods` rows
  (query_by_name uniqueness depends on it), per source.

