## TODO: stalker2-support

Next major game. DECIDED 2026-08-07 after the strategy research sessions; this entry
records the direction and its guardrails so later work does not relitigate them. Like
everything in this file, do not start implementation without the owner explicitly
saying so.

### The decision

- STALKER 2: Heart of Chornobyl (Steam appid 1643320, UE5 - 5.1.x per public info,
  verify the exact version when the parser work starts) is the next game added.
- Ready or Not is the likely game AFTER it - a second consumer for the UE5 pak
  handling, the Nexus flows, conflict detection, and the future mod.io client - but
  it gets its own independent go/no-go (real-install verification, conflict-pain,
  anti-cheat and pak-signature checks) and nothing starts on it until STALKER 2 v1
  has shipped.
- No game is ever added merely to rehearse an API or a source integration. A game
  enters the roster only when supporting it is independently worthwhile; the
  fallback for a game that disappoints is feature-freeze, since public support
  cannot be retracted.

### v1 scope (smallest credible, family-conforming)

- Sources: the existing Nexus integration plus local archive install and
  drag-and-drop. No mod.io and no Steam Workshop in v1. Registry facts verified live
  2026-08-07: domain stalker2heartofchornobyl, numeric gameId 6944 (for the
  SOURCE_REGISTRY numeric_id field), 1,552 published Nexus mods (modCount - lower
  than raw mod-id evidence suggests, since ids run past 2,300 with hidden/removed
  listings). S2 has adult-flagged mods (12 live), so nexus-detail-parity's adult
  handling should land with or before this game; its mods also lean on requirements
  (UE4SS et al), making nexus-feature-parity's dependency work more valuable here
  than for the PAYDAY catalog.
- File-unit target at Stalker2/Content/Paks/~mods with .pak/.ucas/.utoc sidecars
  carried through every op (the Crime Boss sidecar mechanism, not new code).
- The standard engine surface: install, uninstall, enable/disable, update
  detection, health check, reorder.
- Store detection: Steam and Xbox via the existing launchers where the build allows
  it; GOG is a new launcher module (registry keys + Galaxy manifests) and belongs
  to v1 because no current game exercises GOG at all.
- Load order: the community convention is a _{N}_P filename SUFFIX (higher number
  loads later), not the NNN_ prefix the File unit assumes today - see the note in
  game-registry-behavior-hooks.

### Deliberately NOT v1

- Local pak conflict detection for UE5 (which installed mods claim the same packed
  cfg/asset paths) is the differentiating follow-up, not a launch blocker. The S2
  community currently solves this with standalone merge tools, which is the demand
  evidence. It is local-only parsing of the user's own files - no index, no Nexus
  policy exposure - and needs the UE5 format generation noted in pak-analyzer.
- mod.io and Steam Workshop are sequenced by verified user value through the
  acquire-install-split chain (see the 2026-08-07 update there), never
  speculatively.

### Verify on real installations before any implementation

- ~mods loading still intact on the current game patch, and the exact pak/IoStore
  container versions (for the conflict-detection follow-up).
- Sidecar shapes from ~10 real Nexus mods (bare pak vs triplet mix).
- The _{N}_P suffix semantics vs plain alphabetical ordering.
- GOG and Xbox/Game Pass build layouts and whether their file access permits pak
  installs at all.
- GSC's current modding guidance (support.stalker2.com) for anything that
  constrains third-party managers.

